    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Everything is wired correctly and all tests pass. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Summary\n\nOwner deletion is now a **soft-delete**: `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` flags the owner `deleted` and retains the row, `GET` still returns it (with `deleted: true`), and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a `boolean deleted` field (column `deleted`, non-null) with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)`. A new owner defaults to `false`.\n\n2. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct auto-maps it into GET/create responses.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"deleted\", ignore = true)` on the request-body\u2192entity mapping (clients can't set it); the entity\u2192DTO mapping picks it up automatically.\n\n4. **`DeleteOwner`** function \u2014 now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s instead of `repository.delete(owner)`. The existing DELETE pipeline (Load \u2192 Delete \u2192 RespondWithNoContent, 204) is unchanged and still 2xx.\n\n5. **Duplicate/identity checks** \u2014 now skip soft-deleted owners when scanning existing owners:\n   - `RejectDuplicateIdentity` (the 409-blocking household duplicate check \u2014 the key requirement)\n   - `AssignPossibleDuplicate` (soft-duplicate flag)\n   - `AssignNamesakeCount`, `AssignHouseholdSize`, `AssignCustomerCode` (identity-derivation scans)\n\n6. **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN NOT NULL DEFAULT FALSE` so seed rows and new inserts default to `false`.\n\n**Tests:** the full suite (`AcceptanceTest`) is green \u2014 `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, BUILD SUCCESS. The tests exercise both new behaviors: soft-delete flags-and-retains, and a normally-blocking duplicate being allowed once the only match is deleted.\n\nNote: because deleted owners had never existed before this change (delete previously hard-removed the row), the added `isDeleted()` filters are no-ops for all pre-existing behavior \u2014 nothing else could regress.",
